*/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
* Model Number 	  : LM5025 Active Clamp Voltage Mode PWM Controller
* Last Revision Date : Apr 17, 2009
* Revision Number    :1.1
* E-mail feedback 	  : http://wwwd.national.com/feedback/
* Generated from OrCAD Pspice Ver. 10.5, compatible with Ver. 9.2
* Modelled by : Eric Lee,  eric.lee@nsc.com
*/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
*<Introduction >
*This document contains the SPICE model, application example for National Semiconductor's LM5025 
*Active Clamp Voltage Mode PWM Controller. 
*The LM5025 PWM controller contains all of the features necessary to implement power converters 
*utilizing the Active Clamp / Reset technique.
*<LM5025 Model>
*The LM5025 PSPICE Model contains all of the basic features needed to implement single ended primary 
*power converter topologies including;
*- Internal Start-up Bias Regulator 
*- Programmable Line UVLO with Adjustable Hysteresis
*- Voltage Mode Control with Feed-Forward
*- Adjustable Dual Mode Over Crrent Protection 
*- Programmable Overlap or Deadtime 
*- Volt*Second Clamp 
*- Programmable Soft Start 
*- Current Sense with 50nSec Leading Edge Blanking Time for Current Limit
*- Single Resistor Programmable Switching Frequency
*- Oscillator UP/DOWN Sync Capability 
*- 5V Reference Output
*<Assumptions and limitations>
*Model & Example Assumptions;
*- The temperature for this model is 25C
*- ESR and ESL of capacitors are zero.
*- Wire DCR and leakage inductances of transformer are zero.
*- No parasitic elements of package. 
*Some functions/characteristics of LM5025 are not included in this model;
*- Thermal shutdown 
*Some characteristics of LM5025 are included but not optimized
*- Gate driver capability 
*- Power consumption of controller  
*- Synchronous pulse reqirements
*Also AGND&PGND pin of LM5025 is internally tied to GND (node number 0)
*<Note>
*-To run the simulation a simulation profile should be added first--> click 'New Simulation Profile' 
*-The simulation takes around 2~4min per 1mSec simulation on a 1.7GHz machine.
*-User can select LM5025/25A/25B/25C by selecting 'IC' of parameter input. 
*-For LM5025 device, set IC=0
*-For LM5025A device, set IC=1
*-For LM5025B device, set IC=2
*-For LM5025C device, set IC=3
*-SYNC input can be tied to GND through a resistor as it is not used. 
*-Vsupply should have a slope lower than 150V/Sec 
*-Pin name of pin#5 is 'TIME' in the datasheet
*///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

.SUBCKT LM5025 VIN RAMP CS1 CS2 TIMESET REF VCC OUTA OUTB SS COMP RT SYNC UVLO PARAMS: IC=0
Eleb1 F8 0 F9 0 1
