* Model Number 	     : LM5035 PWM Controller with Integrated Half-Bridge and SyncFET Drivers
* Last Revision Date : July 12, 2010
* Revision Number    : 1.0
* E-mail feedback    : http://wwwd.national.com/feedback/
* Generated from Pspice Plugin Ver. 16.2
* Modelled by : Eric Lee,  eric.lee@nsc.com
*////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
* This model has only been tested with Orcad PSPICE.  
* Additional modifications maybe required to work with other SPICE packages
*////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
*<Introduction >
*This document contains the PSPICE model and the simulation circuit example for National Semiconductor's 
*LM5035.
*The LM5035 Half-Bridge Controller/Gate Driver contains all of the features necessary to 
*implement half-bridge topology power converters
*using voltage mode control with line voltage feed-forward.
*<LM5035 Model>
*The LM5035 Model contains all of the basic features including;
*- Voltage Mode with Line Feed-Forward
*- Internal Start-up Bias Regulator
*- Half-Bridge Gate Drivers
*- Synchronous Rectifier Control Outputs with Programmable Delay
*- Single Resistor Programmable Switching Frequency
*- Programmable Soft Start
*- Programmable UVLO and OVP
*- Volt-Second Limiting
*- Cycle-by-Cycle Current Limit
*- Versatile Hiccup mode Current Limit
*- Direct Optocoupler Interface
*- 5V Reference
*<Assumptions and limitations>
*Model & Example Assumptions;
*- The temperature is 25C
*- ESR and ESL of capacitors are zero.
*- Wire DCR and leakage inductances of transformer are zero.
*- No parasitic elements of IC package. 
*Some functions/characteristics of LM5035 are not included in this model;
*- Thermal Shutdown 
*- Oscillator Synchronization
*Some characteristics of LM5035 are included but not optimized
*- Gate driver capability/strength
*- Power consumption of controller  
*- SS discharging time 
*- UVLO shutdown hysteresis (0.1V)
*- 80ns CS delay to output
*Also AGND and PGND pin of LM5035 are internally tied to GND (node number 0)
*<Note>
*- To run the simulation, a simulation profile should be added first. Click 'New Simulation Profile' 
*- The simulation takes around 5~8min actual time per 1ms simulation on a 1.7GHz machine.
*- Vsupply should have a slope lower than 1V/us
*///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
.SUBCKT LM5035 RAMP UVLO OVP COMP RT CS SS DLY RES HB HS HO LO VCC SR2 SR1 REF VIN
