*////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
*<Introduction >
*This document contains the PSPICE model and the simulation circuit example for National Semiconductor's 
*LM5035C.
*The LM5035C Half-Bridge Controller/Gate Driver contains all of the features necessary to implement 
*half-bridge topology power converters
*using voltage mode control with line voltage feed-forward.
*<LM5035C Model>
*The LM5035C Model contains all of the basic features including;
*- Voltage Mode with Line Feed-Forward
*- Internal Start-up Bias Regulator
*- Half-Bridge Gate Drivers
*- Synchronous Rectifier Control Outputs with Programmable Delay
*- Single Resistor Programmable Switching Frequency
*- Programmable Soft Start
*- Programmable UVLO and OVP
*- Volt-Second Limiting
*- Cycle-by-Cycle Current Limit
*- Versatile Hiccup mode Current Limit
*- Direct Optocoupler Interface
*- 5V Reference
*<Assumptions and limitations>
*Model & Example Assumptions;
*- The temperature is 25C
*- ESR and ESL of capacitors are zero.
*- Wire DCR and leakage inductances of transformer are zero.
*- No parasitic elements of IC package. 
*Some functions/characteristics of LM5035C are not included in this model;
*- Thermal Shutdown 
*- Oscillator Synchronization
*Some characteristics of LM5035C are included but not optimized
*- Gate driver capability/strength
*- Power consumption of controller  
*- SS discharging time 
*- UVLO shutdown hysteresis (0.1V)
*- 80ns CS delay to output
*Also AGND and PGND pin of LM5035C are internally tied to GND (node number 0)
*<Note>
*- To run the simulation, a simulation profile should be added first. Click 'New Simulation Profile' 
*- The simulation takes around 4~8min actual time per 1ms simulation on a 1.7GHz machine.
*- Vsupply should have a slope lower than 1V/us
*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
